<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  ASSOCIATED DOMAINS — the iOS half of Universal Links.

	  This file is a TEMPLATE, not the file Xcode compiles. `ios/` holds only
	  HANDOFF.md and this template; the native project is generated by the
	  Capacitor CLI on every run ('cap add ios' / 'cap sync ios'), so anything
	  placed inside ios/App/ is regenerated or overwritten. scripts/ios-associated-domains.mjs
	  copies this file to ios/App/App/App.entitlements after the sync and points
	  the Xcode target's CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS at it. Edit it HERE.

	  Each `applinks:` entry must be a host that serves
	  /.well-known/apple-app-site-association over https with no redirect:

	    fantasysportsnetwork.app      landing project  -> landing/.well-known/…
	    www.fantasysportsnetwork.app  landing project  -> landing/.well-known/…
	    app.fantasysportsnetwork.app  app project      -> .well-known/…

	  All three are listed because all three are reachable in a share: the app
	  builds content links on its own origin (app.), the landing page's connect
	  CTAs live on www., and the apex is what people type. iOS fetches each
	  host's AASA independently — a host missing from this list is a link that
	  opens Safari, and a host listed here without a served AASA is a silent
	  no-op. scripts/check-applinks.mjs pins the two lists to each other.

	  Adding a host is not enough on its own: the App ID in the Apple Developer
	  portal must also carry the Associated Domains capability, which Xcode
	  enables for you on an archive built with -allowProvisioningUpdates.

	  APNs uses the production environment in App Store/TestFlight exports.
	  The exported signature is checked before upload; a profile alone is not enough.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:fantasysportsnetwork.app</string>
		<string>applinks:www.fantasysportsnetwork.app</string>
		<string>applinks:app.fantasysportsnetwork.app</string>
	</array>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
